{"title":"2003 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/e/dae66c1fc9b2b4379efbc4bbea97c50ead1c9226.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2^n}+2^n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"95\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In order for an integer to be divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the integer must be divisible by both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nFor divisibility by 3, note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/c/e3c9640aa77dc4934cc44091e620dc6d8f54892b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is even and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/f/bcf913f68456a152c3f3f568a749231e8090dc63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c36f0b157e8c2fbe0638c2f2b378e08d07695aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> is even for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/7/897470a282b6b85fa5221eacd41369b9a157f491.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/c/e4c6bc4ef6ef87cf3ddec457ba22e8ee05cbb239.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2^n} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" /> for all values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.  Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be an even number.\n</p><p><br />\nFor divisibility by 7, because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/3/433935c5133838eb146dc1aa373291a25f6d01ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^3 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"120\" height=\"19\" />, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/4/e94c8b3a9dfaf0df72bd21b3d73a2d9c6d1124f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{3n} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{7}, 2^{3n+1} \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7}, 2^{3n+2} \\equiv 4 \\pmod{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"439\" height=\"19\" />.  Additionally, by trying small values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/3/053bf3b22c85727325a547f0e11abff7c08cb359.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2^0} \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7}, 2^{2^1} \\equiv 4 \\pmod{7}, 2^{2^2} \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7}, 2^{2^3} \\equiv 4 \\pmod{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"537\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nThus, we suspect that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/2/b1212267326490d535f16029a5cc789ba75df7fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2^n} \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is even and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/1/3b1dc152a0b4efab870dc320cda3ce8c25328e4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2^n} \\equiv 4 \\pmod{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd.  To prove this, we can use <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Induction\" title=\"Induction\">induction</a>.  For the base case, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/8/3c85d98cf99ca47aab7ae16b42ca85805f90574d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2^0} \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"127\" height=\"23\" /> and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/9/a29a1cbfed65deb144d0af6a065cc63fe0c7f240.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2^1} \\equiv 4 \\pmod{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"24\" />.  For the inductive step, assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/1/3b1dc152a0b4efab870dc320cda3ce8c25328e4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2^n} \\equiv 4 \\pmod{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" />.  By using properties of exponents and modular arithmetic, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/acef49f8a4a961d370b07fe0c713d69d5e1d2cb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2^{n+1}} \\equiv 2^{2 \\cdot 2^n} \\equiv (2^{2^n})^2 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"276\" height=\"24\" />.  Additionally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/9/079047bed41054ff6b0c1642626117c9e6c0f4d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2^{n+2}} \\equiv 2^{4 \\cdot 2^n} \\equiv (2^{2^n})^4 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"273\" height=\"23\" />.  The inductive step holds, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/2/b1212267326490d535f16029a5cc789ba75df7fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2^n} \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is even and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/1/3b1dc152a0b4efab870dc320cda3ce8c25328e4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2^n} \\equiv 4 \\pmod{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd.\n</p><p><br />\nBecause we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be even, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/2/b1212267326490d535f16029a5cc789ba75df7fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2^n} \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"20\" />.  Therefore, we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/0/6107b10873b534cfad72bedbe386db31add1e94a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^n \\equiv 4 \\pmod{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/5/5f5cbead4d646c454c8dea87c89076d7f30e961f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\equiv 2 \\pmod{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" />.  In summary, the integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfy the original conditions are in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/f/f2f91b21cfe0f5d439f0ba5fe59586fd7c6c71e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{n = 6n+2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"98\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO\">2003 Pan African MO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_Pan_African_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2003 Pan African MO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pan_African_MO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"Pan African MO Problems and Solutions\"> All Pan African MO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017202629\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.038 seconds\nPreprocess